# KNOWN GAP — an UNNAMED TEMP in MATCH SCRUTINEE POSITION leaks its payload.
# Live at pristine HEAD, no fix applied, no closure anywhere.
#
#     match mkE(mk("hel","lo")):        # unnamed temp  -> 6 B / 1 allocation
#         case E.A(x): print(x)
#
#     E e = mkE(mk("hel","lo"))         # named local   -> CLEAN
#     match e:
#         case E.A(x): print(x)
#
# THE DISCRIMINATOR IS THE UNNAMED TEMP IN SCRUTINEE POSITION -- nothing else.
# The two programs are otherwise identical; binding the scrutinee to a named
# local first is enough to make the leak disappear.
#
# Frames: `str_alloc_copy` <- ... <- `mkE` <- `main`.
#
# ⚠ NOT a closure defect -- distinct from `t0526`, which is closure-capture and
# whose frames go through `__Closure_N__call`. There is no closure here.
#
# ⚠ EXPOSED, NOT INTRODUCED BY ANY IN-FLIGHT FIX. Measured at pristine HEAD.
# The control that removes the extraction entirely (`.is_some()` instead of
# the case binding) ALSO leaks at HEAD with identical frames, which is what
# establishes that the extraction is not the cause.
#
# ⚠ NO GATE SEES THIS. It lands inside `test_option_resource_field`'s own
# shapes, and that fixture uses only STATIC-LITERAL payloads -- `t0036`'s
# named false negative -- so it cannot observe a heap leak. Any net for this
# class must heap-FORCE the payload via a concat function.
#
# ⚠ PROBE HYGIENE, learned the hard way on this defect: under `--sanitize` a
# LEAKING program's stdout is LOST -- LSan does not flush -- so a run that
# leaks shows no output. Do not read "no output" as "the program printed
# nothing"; check the sanitizer summary separately.
#
# INTENDED (asserted by the wired ASan test): rc 0, no leak, both backends,
# regardless of whether the scrutinee is a named local or a temp.
# Measured 2026-08-27 by R45 Track D brief-review pass 9; orchestrator-verified
# with the named-local control run alongside.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

enum E:
    A(String)
    B(int)

E mkE(String s):
    return E.A(s)

void main():
    match mkE(mk("hel", "lo")):
        case E.A(x):
            print(x)
        else:
            print("no")
